       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is well above the maximum for ibuprofen. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided another way\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1600 mg QID, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also want to add a note with the rationale to the order."
